pect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =2, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(2t+4s)\\cdot 2+(6t-2s)\\cdot (-1)+(2st)\\cdot t \\\\  & =4t+8s-6t+2s+2s{t}^{2} \\\\  & =10s-2t+2s{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2(5s-t+s{t}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323420 13194139534968 true] [17592186323419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323421 13194139534968 true] [17592186323419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323422 13194139534968 true] [17592186323419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323423 13194139534968 true] [17592186323419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323424 13194139534968 true] [17592186323419 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534968 true] [17592186323419 1041 "selection" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323419 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323421 13194139534968 true] [17592186323419 1110 #uuid "2d38d470-41a5-5d18-9c6d-0f46200ccd38" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323420 1034 "3s-5t-1" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323420 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534968 true] [17592186323420 1111 #uuid "a5809ec2-a496-5b6b-9be7-47681ddd6d88" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323421 1034 "2(5s-t+s{t}^{2})" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323421 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534968 true] [17592186323421 1111 #uuid "8bf30693-4866-5a63-937c-d6ea81fe9c4d" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323422 1034 "s(t+s)^{2}" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323422 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534968 true] [17592186323422 1111 #uuid "24564973-e0da-5365-a4d4-47755aa07a0c" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323423 1034 "4(st+s-t)" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323423 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534968 true] [17592186323423 1111 #uuid "30c76fc8-8ac2-55a8-a278-c2cfa5863a33" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323424 1034 "t(5-s)^{2}" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323424 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534968 true] [17592186323424 1111 #uuid "74e37fcd-b4b0-5ec1-8ff0-734da93392fa" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323425 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323426 13194139534968 true] [17592186323425 1089 "q-94816" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323425 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534968 true] [17592186323425 1100 "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2{e}^{y}+4z,$ where $x=t{s}^{2},$ $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+{s}^{2})$ and $z={s}^{2}.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323425 1113 #uuid "f54cad8f-6f81-5bf1-9373-fb4d7af3562f" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323425 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-2{e}^{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{t{s}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-2{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+{s}^{2})}=-2({t}^{2}+{s}^{2}), \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =2ts, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =\\frac{2s}{{t}^{2}+{s}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(\\frac{1}{t{s}^{2}})\\cdot 2ts+(-2({t}^{2}+{s}^{2}))\\cdot (\\frac{2s}{{t}^{2}+{s}^{2}})+(4)\\cdot 2s \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-4s+8s \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}+4s \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1+2{s}^{2})}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323427 13194139534968 true] [17592186323426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323428 13194139534968 true] [17592186323426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323429 13194139534968 true] [17592186323426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323430 13194139534968 true] [17592186323426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323431 13194139534968 true] [17592186323426 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534968 true] [17592186323426 1041 "selection" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323426 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323429 13194139534968 true] [17592186323426 1110 #uuid "e52e23f4-47d9-5bf1-b5e3-59f36d43abb3" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323427 1034 "st({s}^{2}{t}^{2}+1)" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534968 true] [17592186323427 1111 #uuid "a631c9b1-f15a-567c-8779-26da12a59286" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323428 1034 "\\frac{1+{t}^{2}}{s}" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323428 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534968 true] [17592186323428 1111 #uuid "371e683f-4245-5dc5-bc94-f0b1e611b893" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323429 1034 "\\frac{2(1+2{s}^{2})}{s}" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534968 true] [17592186323429 1111 #uuid "af0ddd68-d47f-57cc-b0eb-868da8ab44fd" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323430 1034 "\\frac{{t}^{2}-{s}^{2}}{s}" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323430 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534968 true] [17592186323430 1111 #uuid "5f471692-18b5-5e28-80d9-f3cafbcddd2f" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323431 1034 "\\frac{st+1}{2}" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323431 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534968 true] [17592186323431 1111 #uuid "f3115d56-c996-52a9-9fa4-83a40f1f3531" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323432 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323433 13194139534968 true] [17592186323432 1089 "q-95076" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323432 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534968 true] [17592186323432 1100 "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{y},x=2t$ and $y={t}^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323432 1113 #uuid "d7005bf6-3723-544e-bddf-addae8b8b624" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323432 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{e}^{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(2t){e}^{{t}^{2}}=4t{e}^{{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(2t)^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}}=4{t}^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =4t{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\cdot 2+4{t}^{2}{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =8t{e}^{{t}^{2}}+8{t}^{3}{e}^{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =8t(1+{t}^{2}){e}^{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323433 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323434 13194139534968 true] [17592186323433 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323435 13194139534968 true] [17592186323433 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323436 13194139534968 true] [17592186323433 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323437 13194139534968 true] [