rst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s)+(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s})\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s \\\\  & =-2-2\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s} \\\\  & =-2-2{cot}^{2}⁡2s \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323455 13194139534968 true] [17592186323454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323456 13194139534968 true] [17592186323454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323457 13194139534968 true] [17592186323454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323458 13194139534968 true] [17592186323454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323459 13194139534968 true] [17592186323454 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534968 true] [17592186323454 1041 "selection" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323454 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323456 13194139534968 true] [17592186323454 1110 #uuid "ebcd6dbb-dde2-5e3e-b7e9-76d3d882377d" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323455 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡2s+{csc}^{2}⁡2s" 13194139534968 true] [17592186323455 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534968 true] [17592186323455 1111 #uuid "ca1bdaf6-5fbd-5ebd-8385-88367c25d304" 